# C041: Python 3.10-3.11 async exception buffering creates tuples with NULL items
#
# CONFIRMED — static analysis (invalid Python object)
#
# On Python < 3.12 (cursor.c:1738-1746), PyErr_Fetch may return NULL value or
# traceback pointers, but they are inserted with PyTuple_SET_ITEM (stealing,
# no NULL check).  This creates an invalid tuple.  The consumer code
# (cursor.c:1686-1701) checks for NULL fields and replaces with RuntimeError,
# but the intermediate tuple with NULL items is technically invalid and any
# other code touching it would crash.  Runtime testing on Python 3.10 did not
# trigger a crash because most exceptions have non-NULL value/tb.
